= Cecil Parkinson

[? if con_in_government = 0 : A trade spokesman, and one of your most loyal supporters. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and time < 45 : Minister for Trade. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and time >= 45 : Chairman of the Conservative Party. ?] A grammar-school boy from Lancashire who made a fortune in accountancy. Smooth on television and popular in the constituencies.

- @dinners
- @small_business
- @campaign_plan
- @machine
- @root: Return

@dinners
title: Work the business dinners
subtitle: Gain [+ donations + 1 +] resources.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; resources += donations + 1

Parkinson spends a month of evenings in the hotels of the Home Counties. The cheques arrive by the next post.

@small_business
title: Champion small business
view-if: con_in_government = 0
subtitle: The self-employed and white-collar voters warm to us.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); ab_con += 1*(1-dissent); economic_liberalism += 1

Parkinson tours the trading estates promising less paperwork, lower taxes and an end to Labour's price controls.

@campaign_plan
title: Plan the next campaign
subtitle: A broad lift in support, and more during a campaign.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); thatcher_rating += 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent) if in_campaign = 1; c2_con += 2*(1-dissent) if in_campaign = 1

Parkinson draws up the target seats, the poster sites and the leader's tour, and runs the whole operation from Central Office with a computer.

@machine
title: Run the party machine
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: Calms the party and raises a little money.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; loyalist_dissent -= 5; rebellion -= 1; resources += 1

The Party Chairman visits every area office and reassures the agents that the government knows what it's doing. They want to believe him.
